WEBVTT

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:11.230
The first trimester is ending soon...

00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:17.610
I have to admit, I was kind
of depressed at the beginning...

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:20.950
But now that I think about it,
it was over in a flash.

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:26.620
Thanks to my friends,
who I spend a lot of fun times with...

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:29.580
Miki-chan!

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:32.250
Let's eat lunch on the balcony today!

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:34.920
Sure, but isn't it hot up there?

00:00:35.330 --> 00:00:37.300
Hmm, good point...

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:39.170
Hey, Midori-chan!

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:40.880
Midori-chan!

00:00:44.660 --> 00:00:47.560
Sorry, I have work to do after school.

00:00:47.930 --> 00:00:50.640
Come on, can't you make
an exception for me, Midori?

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:54.440
That's the... student council vice-chair.

00:00:55.290 --> 00:00:57.110
I'm sorry I couldn't assist.

00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:00.250
If that's all, I will excuse myself.

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:00.780
Oh...

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:02.660
Come on, let's go.

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:04.780
Huh? Oh... Okay.

00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:49.580
Okay! As we discussed before, we're
trying to make this year's school festival

00:02:49.580 --> 00:02:53.470
truly unique and memorable, so I've
asked you all to come up with some ideas.

00:02:53.930 --> 00:02:55.180
What have you come up with?

00:02:57.270 --> 00:03:00.380
Well, we did jot some stuff down, but...

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:04.570
We couldn't really come up with
anything that unique or memorable.

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:07.110
It's okay! Let's just lay it all out!

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:11.450
If we put our heads together
I'm sure we can think of something.

00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:21.130
What is this...?
It's all so common and overdone...

00:03:21.580 --> 00:03:26.080
Hot dog eating contest...?
Who came up with such a dumb idea...?

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:28.260
Um... you did, Vice-Chair...

00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:28.760
Ugh...

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:33.180
I don't think we can pull off
something completely new.

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:36.870
We should just play it safe,
like the previous years.

00:03:36.870 --> 00:03:37.850
No!

00:03:38.140 --> 00:03:41.930
If we do that,
what's the point of me taking over

00:03:41.930 --> 00:03:43.730
for the chairperson who's still
in the hospital after the accident?!

00:03:44.780 --> 00:03:47.620
Chairperson! Please get well soon.

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:49.070
We're all waiting for you...

00:03:51.070 --> 00:03:54.030
I'm sorry, Shibusawa.
I need you to cover for me.

00:03:55.910 --> 00:04:00.580
I, Shibusawa Ren, will make this
the best school festival ever!

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:04.340
I've taken on the task. Now I have to deliver!

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:14.550
Aoshima-senpai...

00:04:16.350 --> 00:04:20.190
It was when I first joined
the student council...

00:04:20.190 --> 00:04:22.810
Moving on to the next subject...

00:04:22.540 --> 00:04:23.770
Oh.

00:04:24.020 --> 00:04:27.300
Kimura, so you're a humanities-type,
huh? You don't look that way.

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:32.200
Yes, but to be honest, I'm terrible at it.
It's just that math and science are worse.

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:37.350
Hey, Chairperson!
And Kimura-kun! Are you listening?!

00:04:37.350 --> 00:04:41.290
I am, I am. You're taking your job
quite seriously, First-Year Vice-Chair!

00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:46.340
We're in a meeting right now.
Please refrain from talking out of order.

00:04:46.750 --> 00:04:47.500
Gotcha.

00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:54.140
My first impression of Aoshima-senpai was
that he was tall and took nothing seriously.

00:04:54.930 --> 00:04:59.890
But still, somehow he was popular
with both male and female students.

00:04:59.890 --> 00:05:02.060
I hated him.

00:05:04.150 --> 00:05:05.360
Senpai, so...

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:10.300
Why did you run for
student council chairperson?

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:11.700
What's this all of a sudden?

00:05:12.110 --> 00:05:16.750
The student council board members
need to be an example to all students.

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:21.330
But you're never on time
and you bend the rules.

00:05:22.040 --> 00:05:26.290
How do you expect other students to
behave well if you don't take this seriously?

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:29.600
Wow, I'm impressed, Shibusawa!

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:30.260
Huh?

00:05:30.550 --> 00:05:36.720
Well, I've never put any thought into
being an example and behaving and stuff.

00:05:37.510 --> 00:05:38.430
I knew it...

00:05:39.010 --> 00:05:43.440
People just voted for him
because he's popular and fun!

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:47.200
Why am I stuck working
under someone like him...?

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:51.070
But there is a reason why I ran
for student council chairperson.

00:05:52.030 --> 00:05:56.160
I love seeing everyone smile.

00:05:57.620 --> 00:06:01.370
The student council is
a good place to achieve that.

00:06:02.290 --> 00:06:02.870
Here.

00:06:03.950 --> 00:06:08.330
The overview of next year's budget
that you asked Kimura to finish.

00:06:08.330 --> 00:06:13.410
What? It's done already?
Kimura-kun is better than he says!

00:06:13.410 --> 00:06:17.290
No, Tanaka took care of that.

00:06:17.290 --> 00:06:21.540
Tanaka is more detail-oriented.
He's better at this type of stuff.

00:06:21.540 --> 00:06:25.290
On the other hand, Kimura took care of
the negotiations with the sports clubs

00:06:25.290 --> 00:06:30.370
that you asked Tanaka to do.
He's got better people skills.

00:06:30.370 --> 00:06:34.750
Shibusawa, you can do
anything on your own.

00:06:34.750 --> 00:06:41.080
But you're just one small person. There's a
limit to how much you can do by yourself.

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:44.580
Relax, Shibusawa.

00:06:46.160 --> 00:06:49.410
He saw through everything...

00:06:50.620 --> 00:06:56.120
He seemed like he didn't care, but no,
he actually understood everyone.

00:06:57.250 --> 00:07:03.540
Since then, I've followed his lead
and tried to get others to help me.

00:07:03.540 --> 00:07:06.100
But this time...

00:07:06.540 --> 00:07:08.980
...I really need her!

00:07:10.790 --> 00:07:14.910
Wow, so you were the student council
chairperson in middle school?

00:07:14.910 --> 00:07:17.110
Wow... Impressive, Midori-chan.

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:21.160
It's really not. I just got pulled in by a
<i>senpai</i> who was good at convincing people

00:07:21.160 --> 00:07:23.200
and couldn't find a way out after that.

00:07:23.200 --> 00:07:26.040
Aren't you going to join the
student council here in high school?

00:07:26.040 --> 00:07:28.910
No. I've got other things I want to do.

00:07:28.910 --> 00:07:31.250
What other things?!

00:07:31.250 --> 00:07:34.700
Senpai? What are you doing here?

00:07:34.700 --> 00:07:38.750
The student council keeps track
of all the places where students work!

00:07:38.750 --> 00:07:46.290
Hey, Midori. Can you help me prepare
the school festival? I need your help!

00:07:46.290 --> 00:07:52.500
Um, I was meaning to ask,
what exactly is your relationship...?

00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:55.540
We went to middle school together.

00:07:55.540 --> 00:08:01.410
We were a team back then.
We ran every event in the entire school!

00:08:01.410 --> 00:08:06.120
So this is the "<i>senpai</i> who is
good at convincing people."

00:08:06.120 --> 00:08:12.450
Come on! If you lend me a hand,
I will make sure you win the next election.

00:08:12.450 --> 00:08:17.000
Then the two of us can run
this school like we did before!

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:20.500
I've already turned down that offer before.

00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:22.750
I'm too preoccupied with personal matters.

00:08:22.750 --> 00:08:25.500
I don't have time to work
for the student council.

00:08:25.500 --> 00:08:31.120
I don't know what it is you want to do,
but you can do part-time work in college!

00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:33.750
Don't waste your time trying
to make some quick cash.

00:08:33.750 --> 00:08:35.830
Let's do something you can only do now!

00:08:35.830 --> 00:08:36.870
Come on!

00:08:36.870 --> 00:08:41.370
Money isn't the only reason I work here.

00:08:41.370 --> 00:08:46.450
Huh? Not for money? Then why?

00:08:46.450 --> 00:08:49.910
For... my dream.

00:08:49.910 --> 00:08:51.870
Dream...?

00:08:51.870 --> 00:08:55.660
What's your dream?

00:08:55.660 --> 00:09:02.000
I want to make games.
My dream is to become a board game author.

00:09:04.410 --> 00:09:06.200
Board games...?

00:09:09.080 --> 00:09:14.750
You have to be kidding!
I was expecting anything, but board games...?

00:09:14.750 --> 00:09:15.830
What's wrong with that?

00:09:15.830 --> 00:09:20.250
Huh? Of course,
there's so much wrong with that!

00:09:20.250 --> 00:09:25.870
Board games are totally outdated.
Who even plays those anymore?

00:09:25.870 --> 00:09:28.370
Midori, what's gotten into you?

00:09:28.370 --> 00:09:34.870
Just drop that worthless thing
and come join me! I promise you'll do well.

00:09:34.870 --> 00:09:37.620
It's not worthless!

00:09:37.620 --> 00:09:39.080
Miki...

00:09:39.080 --> 00:09:40.870
What's your deal?

00:09:40.870 --> 00:09:44.830
Board games... aren't worthless...

00:09:44.830 --> 00:09:50.000
I'm talking to Midori right now.
Can you stay out of it, outsider?

00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:52.660
We're not outsiders! We're friends!

00:09:52.660 --> 00:09:58.410
Like Miki-chan said, board games aren't
worthless, and they're not outdated!

00:09:58.410 --> 00:10:00.700
They're really, really fun!

00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:03.290
Miki... Aya...

00:10:03.290 --> 00:10:06.790
Heh! I have no interest
in how "fun" it might be!

00:10:06.790 --> 00:10:11.870
Games in general aren't necessary in life;
you can take them or leave them.

00:10:11.870 --> 00:10:14.040
That's what I mean by worthless!

00:10:14.040 --> 00:10:18.500
Midori has real talents; they should be used
to do something with actual value!

00:10:18.500 --> 00:10:24.000
She and I ruled over middle
school together. I know her best!

00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:26.950
I...

00:10:26.950 --> 00:10:31.000
I'm in the student council because
I want to see everyone smile!

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:34.080
Midori! I thought you felt the same way, too!

00:10:36.790 --> 00:10:40.660
Value is determined differently
from person to person.

00:10:40.660 --> 00:10:45.540
What could be trash to someone
might be a treasure to others.

00:10:45.540 --> 00:10:52.000
Forcing those value judgments on others
will never help us reach an answer.

00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:54.250
Yes... this is it.

00:10:54.250 --> 00:10:56.660
Not budging at all to a <i>senpai</i> 's pressure.

00:10:56.660 --> 00:11:03.580
Perfect composure, control, and decision-making
maintained, even when taunted...

00:11:03.580 --> 00:11:08.080
She has to be the one to take over after me!

00:11:08.080 --> 00:11:11.580
I'll let you know,
I'm not leaving until you say yes!

00:11:11.580 --> 00:11:16.160
That could be an issue...
It's around the time things get busy here.

00:11:18.700 --> 00:11:21.950
Tell you what, Senpai.
Why don't we play for this?

00:11:21.950 --> 00:11:23.290
Play?

00:11:23.290 --> 00:11:29.160
We can play a game together.
If you can beat me, I will obey you.

00:11:29.160 --> 00:11:34.040
But if you lose, you have to give up on me.

00:11:34.040 --> 00:11:36.540
Fine, whatever you say.

00:11:36.540 --> 00:11:39.330
So what game are we playing?

00:11:40.330 --> 00:11:41.000
<i>6 Nimmt</i>!

00:11:41.750 --> 00:11:44.130
I'll take you on in this game, Senpai!

00:11:51.750 --> 00:11:54.160
<i>6 Nimmt</i> is a simple game.

00:11:54.160 --> 00:11:57.790
First, we shuffle a deck of cards
with the numbers 1 through 104 on them.

00:11:57.790 --> 00:12:02.540
We deal ten cards to each player
and leave the rest in a deck.

00:12:02.540 --> 00:12:07.910
Draw four cards from the deck
and place them faceup on the table.

00:12:07.910 --> 00:12:09.790
Next, how to play.

00:12:09.790 --> 00:12:12.700
Every player chooses a card
from their hand and puts it facedown.

00:12:12.700 --> 00:12:17.250
When everyone is ready,
reveal the cards at the same time.

00:12:17.250 --> 00:12:22.500
Starting from the smallest number, line
the cards up next to the cards on the table.

00:12:22.500 --> 00:12:26.910
You have to put each card
after the number it is closest to.

00:12:26.910 --> 00:12:30.040
So in this example,
the cards are laid out like...

00:12:31.830 --> 00:12:33.000
...this.

00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:34.700
Oh, I see.

00:12:34.700 --> 00:12:35.750
And then?

00:12:35.750 --> 00:12:39.290
This process is repeated until
we play every card in our hand, but...

00:12:39.290 --> 00:12:41.290
...the key is the sixth card.

00:12:41.290 --> 00:12:47.080
The person who plays the sixth card
in a row must take the five other cards.

00:12:47.080 --> 00:12:51.700
The card that was played
gets placed at the front.

00:12:51.700 --> 00:12:53.910
What happens when you get a card?

00:12:53.910 --> 00:12:56.000
Do you see the cow symbols on the card?

00:12:56.000 --> 00:12:57.540
Oh, yeah!

00:12:57.540 --> 00:13:03.500
After playing all ten cards, the person
with the largest number of cows loses.

00:13:03.500 --> 00:13:05.700
Huh? The person who gets the cows loses?

00:13:05.700 --> 00:13:11.620
Yes. This game is not about taking cows,
it's about forcing cows on other people.

00:13:11.620 --> 00:13:13.370
Forcing cows on people?

00:13:15.290 --> 00:13:21.450
One more thing. If the card you play
is smaller than all other cards in play,

00:13:21.450 --> 00:13:27.080
you pick a row of your choice
and take all the cards in that row.

00:13:27.080 --> 00:13:29.750
You can choose any row?

00:13:29.750 --> 00:13:34.370
Yes. So in most cases you want
to choose the row with the least cows.

00:13:34.370 --> 00:13:35.910
That's all?

00:13:35.910 --> 00:13:38.040
Yes, those are the rules.

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:44.700
Huh, what a simple game.
So you'll really do as I say if I win?

00:13:44.700 --> 00:13:46.500
Yes, I promise.

00:13:46.500 --> 00:13:48.910
Fine then, let's do this!

00:13:48.910 --> 00:13:50.420
Yes! Let's play!

00:13:53.160 --> 00:13:56.220
Okay, everyone choose a card
and place it facedown...

00:13:57.680 --> 00:14:00.350
Flip at the same time, go!

00:14:02.810 --> 00:14:05.100
If we lay these out in order...

00:14:05.870 --> 00:14:08.150
Wow, it's quite unbalanced.

00:14:08.540 --> 00:14:11.330
Because there are only four players,
the first turn is always safe.

00:14:11.330 --> 00:14:13.160
Second turn and onwards
is where it really begins.

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:15.530
Ready? Here we go!

00:14:16.620 --> 00:14:20.250
Wow, row two is already one card away!

00:14:20.250 --> 00:14:21.410
You're right!

00:14:23.200 --> 00:14:25.620
This is super easy.

00:14:25.620 --> 00:14:30.660
There's a 48 on the table,
so this is 100 percent safe...

00:14:30.660 --> 00:14:34.750
All that talk about dreams from Midori
kind of got my expectations up, but...

00:14:34.750 --> 00:14:38.160
What's so fun about this simple number game?

00:14:38.160 --> 00:14:42.580
Midori, I'll beat you and
wake you up to the real world!

00:14:42.580 --> 00:14:44.520
Ready? Here we go!

00:14:46.200 --> 00:14:50.120
So I'll put this 49 behind the 48...

00:14:50.120 --> 00:14:51.450
Wait, Senpai.

00:14:51.450 --> 00:14:52.580
Huh?

00:14:52.580 --> 00:14:58.950
I played a seven. It's smaller than all
the other numbers, so I'll take a row.

00:14:58.950 --> 00:14:59.870
What...?

00:14:59.870 --> 00:15:03.370
So I'll take this 48...

00:15:03.370 --> 00:15:07.120
What?! So my 49 is...

00:15:09.370 --> 00:15:12.160
Oh, look, Senpai, your card is the sixth one.

00:15:12.160 --> 00:15:15.410
Please take the other five.

00:15:15.410 --> 00:15:17.260
What the heck?!

00:15:17.580 --> 00:15:21.200
Failing hard on a card you
thought was completely safe...

00:15:21.200 --> 00:15:25.750
...that dramatic turn of events is what
makes <i>6 Nimmt</i> so exciting, Senpai.

00:15:25.750 --> 00:15:28.040
Midori-chan isn't pulling any punches...

00:15:28.040 --> 00:15:29.540
Yeah...

00:15:29.540 --> 00:15:33.500
She got me... That was supposed
to be completely safe...

00:15:33.500 --> 00:15:36.370
I didn't know such a move was possible...

00:15:36.370 --> 00:15:38.610
Okay, next move.

00:15:40.040 --> 00:15:44.580
What is this...? All of a sudden
it feels like no card is safe at all...

00:15:44.580 --> 00:15:47.000
This game is scary!

00:15:47.330 --> 00:15:49.170
Come on, Senpai, hurry!

00:15:50.330 --> 00:15:52.630
But... it's fun!

00:15:55.370 --> 00:16:01.870
The fourth row is... still safe. I can do this!

00:16:01.870 --> 00:16:03.140
Ready, go!

00:16:06.790 --> 00:16:08.790
Wait, what?

00:16:08.790 --> 00:16:10.450
Yes, here.

00:16:10.450 --> 00:16:14.440
Senpai, your 74 is the sixth. You fail again.

00:16:14.790 --> 00:16:16.790
Um, I'm sorry...

00:16:16.790 --> 00:16:19.860
Don't apologize.
It's just the way this game is played.

00:16:22.830 --> 00:16:24.200
Ready, go!

00:16:24.200 --> 00:16:26.500
What?! Again?!

00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:28.000
Ready, go!

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:29.920
Oh, no! Now I failed!

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:28.870
Yes!

00:16:34.540 --> 00:16:37.340
I got... two cows.

00:16:37.620 --> 00:16:41.250
I got seven. What about you, Miki-chan?

00:16:41.250 --> 00:16:43.260
I got four cows...

00:16:45.450 --> 00:16:47.680
So, Senpai, what was your score?

00:16:48.910 --> 00:16:50.560
Heh! So what?

00:16:52.160 --> 00:16:54.870
Yeah, yeah, sure, whatever, I lose!

00:16:54.870 --> 00:16:58.450
I, Shibusawa Ren,
won't hide the fact that I've lost.

00:16:58.450 --> 00:17:00.900
I also admit that this is a fun game.

00:17:02.450 --> 00:17:04.080
But still!

00:17:04.080 --> 00:17:08.040
Why should you, Midori, have to
be the one making these games?!

00:17:08.040 --> 00:17:09.000
Games...

00:17:10.200 --> 00:17:16.290
Games are a bridge that connect
people across borders and generations.

00:17:16.290 --> 00:17:18.870
Those are the words of Kramer,
the person who made <i>6 Nimmt</i> .

00:17:20.500 --> 00:17:23.660
Games have a long history, longer than books.

00:17:23.660 --> 00:17:29.290
Since ancient times, games have connected,
excited, and brought happiness to people.

00:17:29.290 --> 00:17:36.910
I believe games are very precious--
something inseparable from humanity.

00:17:36.910 --> 00:17:40.290
Senpai, you asked me earlier...

00:17:40.290 --> 00:17:44.330
I'm in the student council because
I want to see everyone smile!

00:17:44.330 --> 00:17:47.240
Midori! I thought you felt the same way, too!

00:17:47.870 --> 00:17:51.580
I want to make everyone smile through games!

00:17:52.160 --> 00:17:53.210
Midori-chan!

00:17:52.160 --> 00:17:53.210
Midori-chan!

00:17:54.910 --> 00:17:59.130
I'm never going to give up!

00:17:59.370 --> 00:18:02.010
Midori, you idiot! Idiot! Idiot!

00:18:04.200 --> 00:18:07.830
She took off... Were we mean to her?

00:18:07.830 --> 00:18:09.660
Is she going to be okay, Midori-chan?

00:18:09.660 --> 00:18:13.410
It's fine. It'll take a lot more
than that to really bring her down.

00:18:13.410 --> 00:18:17.820
Rather, it might ignite her passion
and help her succeed with the festival.

00:18:17.820 --> 00:18:19.000
That's the kind of person she is.

00:18:19.000 --> 00:18:20.820
Hey, did she come back?

00:18:23.750 --> 00:18:25.450
Oh, Manager...

00:18:25.450 --> 00:18:28.120
Don't scare us like that!

00:18:28.120 --> 00:18:30.990
Seriously? That totally wasn't my fault...

00:18:33.040 --> 00:18:37.960
Fine, Midori!
If that's what you want, then so be it!

00:18:38.870 --> 00:18:43.840
I can do this without you.
I can make this festival a massive success!

00:18:47.370 --> 00:18:50.160
Ugh, I forgot to get
light bulbs for the restroom.

00:18:50.160 --> 00:18:51.750
Shall I go get some?

00:18:51.750 --> 00:18:52.910
Yeah, thanks.

00:18:52.910 --> 00:18:55.290
I guess we should get going, too, then...

00:18:55.290 --> 00:18:58.870
Yeah, let's go home! We played a lot.

00:19:01.160 --> 00:19:03.910
Midori-chan, you want to be a game author?

00:19:03.910 --> 00:19:06.080
I don't know if I can, but yeah.

00:19:06.080 --> 00:19:08.790
Since when?

00:19:08.790 --> 00:19:12.000
It was when I was in sixth grade...

00:19:12.000 --> 00:19:13.830
My brother brought me along...

00:19:13.830 --> 00:19:15.700
Hey, Manager!

00:19:15.700 --> 00:19:18.630
Hey, Ono-kun. And...

00:19:19.000 --> 00:19:20.000
Who's the young lady?

00:19:20.000 --> 00:19:21.330
She's my little sister.

00:19:21.330 --> 00:19:24.340
We were playing <i>Catan</i> together,
and she got hooked.

00:19:24.910 --> 00:19:28.790
She insisted on coming here and
wouldn't shut up about it, so I brought her.

00:19:28.790 --> 00:19:34.700
Hmm, <i>Catan</i>, at her age? Impressive.
Perhaps gaming runs in your family.

00:19:34.700 --> 00:19:37.040
Welcome, young lady.

00:19:37.040 --> 00:19:38.790
Take your time!

00:19:38.790 --> 00:19:41.750
Come on, say hi.

00:19:41.750 --> 00:19:45.700
Thank you, sir, for looking after
my idiot brother all the time.

00:19:45.700 --> 00:19:49.000
My name is Ono Midori. Your shop is lovely.

00:19:49.000 --> 00:19:50.830
Wait, so...

00:19:50.830 --> 00:19:53.200
...that's how you met the manager?

00:19:53.200 --> 00:19:54.250
Yes.

00:19:54.250 --> 00:19:56.450
From such a young age...

00:19:56.450 --> 00:19:59.870
After that, I went to the shop
a few more times with my brother,

00:19:59.870 --> 00:20:02.500
and the three of us played a lot of games.

00:20:02.500 --> 00:20:04.160
Then, one time...

00:20:04.160 --> 00:20:07.410
Gotcha! I win, Manager!

00:20:07.410 --> 00:20:08.870
Yeah...

00:20:08.870 --> 00:20:15.120
Hmm? Hey, young lady.
Didn't you enjoy <i>Beat the Buzzard</i> ?

00:20:15.120 --> 00:20:17.580
Oh, I certainly did!

00:20:17.580 --> 00:20:23.540
The rules are so simple, but I've never
played a game where I had to think so much.

00:20:23.540 --> 00:20:26.450
Who came up with this game?

00:20:26.450 --> 00:20:31.620
The person who made this game
must be a real genius!

00:20:31.620 --> 00:20:35.120
In Germany, people who design
games are referred to as authors.

00:20:36.370 --> 00:20:41.040
See how each game box
features the name of the author?

00:20:41.040 --> 00:20:47.290
Like people who write novels and manga,
game authors take pride in their creations.

00:20:47.290 --> 00:20:49.290
Game author...

00:20:49.290 --> 00:20:52.580
But this isn't a long-standing
tradition or anything like that.

00:20:52.580 --> 00:20:58.700
In the past, game authors were just
one craftsman in a game company.

00:20:58.700 --> 00:21:03.910
The person who worked hard to
improve the visibility of game authors

00:21:03.910 --> 00:21:08.790
and win many rights for them is
the author of this game, Alex Randolph.

00:21:08.790 --> 00:21:13.370
He is the first person who put the name
of the author on the game's box.

00:21:13.370 --> 00:21:17.620
It later on became a convention
in German games.

00:21:17.620 --> 00:21:21.000
Getting your name printed on a box...

00:21:21.000 --> 00:21:23.620
Do you know what that means?

00:21:23.620 --> 00:21:26.500
From that moment on, games became not
just products manufactured by a company--

00:21:26.500 --> 00:21:29.160
they became works of art by an author.

00:21:32.000 --> 00:21:35.830
From products to art... That's nice!

00:21:35.830 --> 00:21:39.120
I know, right? That's when I decided...

00:21:39.120 --> 00:21:41.810
...to become a game author myself!

00:21:43.330 --> 00:21:45.480
That's my dream!

00:21:47.450 --> 00:21:49.080
Is it weird?

00:21:49.080 --> 00:21:51.200
No! It's great!

00:21:51.200 --> 00:21:54.280
Midori-chan, I know you
can make a great game!

00:21:55.250 --> 00:21:59.290
Thanks. I always thought,
"once I get into high school,

00:21:59.290 --> 00:22:02.910
I should work on pursuing
this dream and make it a reality."

00:22:02.910 --> 00:22:05.290
Game... author...

00:23:37.950 --> 00:23:41.350
We went to Kanazawa during summer break.

00:23:41.830 --> 00:23:44.040
We found this game at the inn.

00:23:44.040 --> 00:23:46.310
I feel like I've played this game before...
